{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1362963-wizened-survival-tactics-every-day-items-that-can-be-made-edible","id":1362963,"title":"Wizened Survival Tactics: Every day items that can be made edible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-23T15:08:03-08:00","id":1362963,"title":"Wizened Survival Tactics: Every day items that can be made edible","content":"So, in pondering how my Wizened Changeling manages to get from the scrapyard he finds himself in (long story) to the Freehold he\u2019d start out in whatever game I play him in, I got to wondering how he managed to survive the journey. I have discussed before the idea of a Wizened using their Blessing to turn mundane objects into food (and vice versa), and now I\u2019m pondering on how he could have done this in a travelling setting. This is what I\u2019ve come up with thus far;<br /> <br /> Paper, plastic wrapping and cardboard with scissors, turning them into lettuce/spinach, cheese, meat and bread/pita (corrugated cardboard preferable for thickness)<br /> Wood with a hand saw of some sort, turning it into cheese, bread and meat<br /> String, rope and or plastic bindings, turning them into noodles of some sort<br /> <br /> Fortunately a multitool would work well to let him do this, though it\u2019d probably take a lot more work than if he had more dedicated tools. Any other items and or foods that could be made in this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T01:23:34-08:00","id":1363040,"title":"","content":"They could have a fruitcake that they made edible with their power.<br /> <br /> Cotton into cotton candy? Glass stones into hard candy and jellybeans?<br /> <br /> Is there anything really stopping a Wizened from turning already extant but spoiled food into fresher versions of the same? It would make scrounging through dumpsters easier if they could turn bad food into good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T01:58:22-08:00","id":1363046,"title":"","content":"The qualifier for the Wizened Blessing is that they work one material into another through natural processes - working metal with a hammer into a new shape, or spinning straw into string. True, you can eschew proper tools in order to make it faster, easier (as well as costlier and less likely to stand up to rigours of use), but the principles is the same; take object, use tools you would to work it into a new shape/form, get something different out of it.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s my reasoning behind paper and cardboard being viable materials for the process with just scissors, since paper can be remade into many different things (such as signs or art) simply by cutting them up. As for spoiled food into mundane food, I don\u2019t know about that - food doesn\u2019t tend to be made into something else constructively beyond pig meal or compost. Not impossible to work with under these circumstances, but it would require a different method for sure and definitely require ST approval.<br /> <br /> As for your other examples, I feel that cotton to cotton candy could work, since cotton is used for a number of things including crafts and making things like string, but glass stones not so much unless it involves hot glue and a collage.<br /> <br /> I do appreciate the feedback though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}